# Native App — Context

## Status
Active development. UI/UX fixes in progress.

## Stack
- React Native + Expo (bare managed)
- NativeWind (TailwindCSS for RN) — theme classes (dark/light) applied via root `View className`
- Redux Toolkit + redux-persist
- React Hook Form + Zod
- react-native-toast-message (global `<Toaster />` in App.tsx; modals include own `<Toast />`)
- `@gym/shared` for DTO types

## Theme System
- 3 themes: `light`, `dark`, `amoled` — Redux `state.theme.theme`
- 4 style modes: `minimal`, `glass`, `clay`, `liquid-glass` — Redux `state.theme.styleMode`
- NativeWind color vars: `text-foreground`, `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `text-muted-foreground`, etc.
- Direct style: `colors.foreground`, `colors.background`, `colors.card`, etc. from `useTheme()` hook
- `themeColors` constant in `src/constants/colors.ts` — light/dark/amoled palettes
- **High-Level UI/UX Professionalization Rule (Theme Inversion Fix)**: NativeWind v4 CSS variables (e.g., `bg-card`, `text-foreground`) can fail to cascade reliably on React Native when toggling themes, resulting in dark components in light mode or eye-straining white components. **Always use explicit inline styles for colors** (e.g., `style={{ backgroundColor: colors.card, color: colors.foreground }}`) derived from `useTheme().colors` on core primitive components (`Card`, `Button`, `Input`, `PageHeader`, `ScreenWrapper`) instead of relying solely on Tailwind CSS classes for dynamic coloring.

## Key Files
- `App.tsx` — root navigator, `<Toaster />` outside navigator
- `src/constants/colors.ts` — `themeColors` object (light/dark/amoled palettes)
- `src/components/ui/Input.tsx` — theme-aware input: `isDark ? bg-white/10 : bg-black/5`. Uses `useTheme()`. Text color via inline style.
- `src/components/ui/Card.tsx` — glass/clay/minimal/default variants; uses `colors.card`; Android glass fallback at `rgba(*,*,0.92)` light / `rgba(*,*,0.90)` dark
- `src/components/ui/Toaster.tsx` — global toast config; positioned `topOffset` from safe area insets
- `src/components/layout/Footer.tsx` — brand + quick links + legal section. Email link: `Linking.openURL('mailto:contact@valorfitness.com')`.
- `src/components/layout/AppDock.tsx` — renders `FloatingDock` or `PublicFloatingDock`
- `src/features/public/publicApi.ts` — `listPublicPlans()`, `submitPublicInquiry()`
- `src/features/members/memberApi.ts` — CRUD + QR + login; phone sent combined (prefix+number)
- `src/features/memberships/membershipApi.ts` — `cancelSubscription(memberId, subscriptionId)`

## Error Parsing Pattern (standard)
All forms use this helper to extract API error messages:
```ts
function parseApiError(error: any): string {
  const data = error?.response?.data;
  if (data?.message && typeof data.message === 'string') return data.message;
  if (Array.isArray(data?.message)) return data.message.join(', ');
  if (data?.error && typeof data.error === 'string') return data.error;
  if (error?.message && typeof error.message === 'string') return error.message;
  return 'An unexpected error occurred. Please try again.';
}
```
Toast pattern: `{ text1: 'Short title', text2: parseApiError(error), visibilityTime: 5000 }`

## Strong Password Regex (active in ChangePasswordModal)
```
/^(?=.*[a-z])(?=.*[A-Z])(?=.*\d)(?=.*[@$!%*?&])[A-Za-z\d@$!%*?&]{8,}$/
```
Requires: min 8 chars, 1 uppercase, 1 lowercase, 1 number, 1 special char.

## Phone Prefix Pattern (MemberFormModal)
- Dropdown: `PHONE_PREFIXES = ['+91', '+1', '+44', '+971', ...]`
- Default: `+91`
- Combined value sent: `${phonePrefix}${phone}` (e.g., `+919876543210`)
- `extractPhoneNumber(fullPhone)` splits on edit mode

## Completed Fixes (this session)

### 0. TypeScript Type-Checking Errors
- Resolved 61 TypeScript errors across 22 files.
- Removed unused variables/imports (`TS6133`, `TS6196`).
- Fixed type mismatches and missing properties in `themeColors` (`TS2339`).
- Replaced unused variables with `_` prefix or removed them completely to pass strict `bun run typecheck`.

### 1. DownloadAppScreen
- Updated Android security disclaimer copy to be more explicit about safety and privacy policy.

### 2. SettingsScreen
- Moved the Theme toggle (Light, Dark, AMOLED, System Default) out of the header and into a prominent button at the top of the UI Styling card.

### 3. MemberFormModal & StaffFormModal
- Replaced basic error handling with an improved `parseApiError` that can handle arrays (to correctly map Zod `400` validation errors).
- Added `topOffset={60}` to `<Toast />` so notifications show correctly over modals on Android.

### 4. MemberLoginScreen & LoginScreen
- Added the strict strong password regex to the login validation schemas.
- Removed artificial `setTimeout` latency during the login passkey phase.

### 5. PublicHomeScreen
- Replaced `toLocaleDateString` with manual Date formatting to prevent Hermes engine crashes on Android.
- Added explicit error states for `listPublicPlans` instead of failing silently.

### 6. Footer
- Added `contact@valorfitness.com` email link to the legal section.
- Reduced the dock spacer (`h-10` to `h-4`) for a tighter layout.

### 7. Input
- Fixed theme color inversion by replacing Tailwind background classes with explicit inline styling (`colors.input` or manual rgba) based on `isDark`.

## Identified Known Issues (future work)
- Staff creation requires user UUID — poor UX; consider email-lookup endpoint
- `ChangePasswordModal` uses `presentationStyle="pageSheet"` which may clip Toast on iOS in some cases
- Passkey flow in MemberLoginScreen is simulated (no real WebAuthn on mobile RN)
- PublicHomeScreen plans: no client-side cache, re-fetches on every mount
